meta {
  name: Add assignee
  type: http
  seq: 9
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/issues/{{issueId}}/assignees
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "userId": "{{memberUserId}}"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
}

docs {
  Anyone who can see the project - there is no separate "assign" permission. Needs issueId from
  Create issue and memberUserId from Projects/Add project member.

  The person has to be able to open the project, or the board would carry work owned by somebody
  who gets a 404 on the issue. A workspace member who is not on a private project, and a user id
  that belongs to nobody, both answer 409 ASSIGNEE_WITHOUT_PROJECT_ACCESS - the same answer on
  purpose, so this cannot be used to find out which accounts exist.

  Running it twice is fine: the second call returns the existing assignment rather than 409.
}
